event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":84,"item_id":"rs_0186412807acc3a9016aca51af2d08819594453d3c7e9ef800","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Planning migration tests**\n\nI’m considering how to handle the migration tests. I need to add the existing test sequence to the archive before making any changes. It seems leveraging SQLite could be useful to create a pre-start for the existing setup. I think it’s ideal to have a minimal pre-created database before starting to change the original expectations. I should also plan to implement a standalone test for the migration separately. That's important!"}

